{
  "id": "f7787f70-07f6-401e-9926-1249c66cb212",
  "productId": "openmrs",
  "title": "Payment Mode Files",
  "updatedAt": 1793522798917,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "Nei9SC9Mm8BS16ug",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "If I wanted to add a new payment mode in the billing system, which files across the repositories would I need to touch?",
      "generation": "g-ab363e",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Payment modes are a **metadata entity, not a hardcoded enum** — they are managed at runtime through a CRUD UI in the frontend and a REST resource in the backend. So \"adding a new payment mode\" (e.g. Mobile Money) is mostly a *data* operation done through the existing UI/REST API, and requires no code change. You only touch code if you want to add a *capability* to payment modes (new attribute, new behaviour, seeded defaults).",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## What already works with no code change",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Create/read/delete flow is generic:",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- **Backend model** — `PaymentMode` is a metadata type with `name`, `description`, `sortOrder` and a list of `attributeTypes` [1]. Any new mode is created by instantiating this class.\n- **Service + DAO** — `PaymentModeService` [2] and `HibernatePaymentModeDAOImpl` [3] are name-agnostic; they never branch on a mode name.\n- **REST endpoint** — `PaymentModeResource` exposes `/billing/paymentMode` with `uuid`, `name`, `description`, `sortOrder`, `attributeTypes` [4].\n- **Hibernate mapping** — table `cashier_payment_mode`, already mapped generically [5].\n- **Frontend CRUD** — the payment-modes config page and the add/edit modal post `{name, description}` to `paymentMode` src/billable-services/payment-mode-form.modal.tsx (file at `src/billable-services/payment-modes/payment-mode-form.modal.tsx`), with `createPaymentMode`/`updatePaymentMode` [6].",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4,
            5,
            6
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## Files to touch only if you change behaviour",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "1. **Backend model/mapping** — add fields to `PaymentMode` [7] and its `many-to-one`/column mappings [8]. New attribute support extends `PaymentModeAttributeType` [9].\n2. **REST representation** — expose any new property in `getRepresentationDescription` [10].\n3. **Frontend payload/type** — `PaymentModePayload` [11] and the `PaymentMode` interface [12].\n4. **Frontend form** — the schema/defaults in the modal src/billable-services/payment-modes/payment-mode-form.modal.tsx; the dropdowns that consume modes need no change because they iterate the fetched list src/invoice/payments/payment-form/payment-form.component.tsx.\n5. **Where a mode becomes a payment** — `Payment` is parameterised by `PaymentMode`, so payment attributes are driven by the mode's attribute types api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/model/Payment.java. Genuinely new *behaviour* (e.g. an external gateway) belongs here.\n6. **Demo/seed data** — the e2e helper looks the mode up by name `'Cash'` e2e/commands/billing-operations.ts; if you seed defaults, adjust this.\n7. **Docs** — the O3 docs repo has no payment-mode material, so a new page would be new content, not an edit (no existing file to cite).",
          "citations": [
            7,
            8,
            9,
            10,
            11,
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## Repositories you do NOT need to touch",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- `openmrs-module-fhir2` — no payment-mode references.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-management` and `openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib` — no `paymentMode` references at all.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "```archify\n{\"schema_version\":1,\"diagram_type\":\"architecture\",\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Payment mode touch points\"},\"components\":[{\"id\":\"pm_ui\",\"type\":\"frontend\",\"label\":\"Payment-modes config UI\",\"sublabel\":\"billing-app\",\"row\":0,\"col\":0},{\"id\":\"pay_form\",\"type\":\"frontend\",\"label\":\"Payment form dropdown\",\"sublabel\":\"billing-app\",\"row\":1,\"col\":0},{\"id\":\"rest\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"PaymentModeResource\",\"sublabel\":\"/billing/paymentMode\",\"row\":0,\"col\":1},{\"id\":\"service\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"PaymentModeService\",\"sublabel\":\"module-billing\",\"row\":1,\"col\":1},{\"id\":\"dao\",\"type\":\"backend\",\"label\":\"PaymentModeDAO\",\"sublabel\":\"Hibernate\",\"row\":2,\"col\":1},{\"id\":\"db\",\"type\":\"database\",\"label\":\"cashier_payment_mode\",\"sublabel\":\"Bill.hbm.xml\",\"row\":3,\"col\":1}],\"connections\":[{\"from\":\"pm_ui\",\"to\":\"rest\",\"label\":\"create/edit/delete\"},{\"from\":\"pay_form\",\"to\":\"rest\",\"label\":\"list modes\"},{\"from\":\"rest\",\"to\":\"service\",\"label\":\"CRUD\"},{\"from\":\"service\",\"to\":\"dao\",\"label\":\"persist\"},{\"from\":\"dao\",\"to\":\"db\",\"label\":\"map\"}]}\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Bottom line:** to *add* a mode, use the config UI or POST `/billing/paymentMode` — no files change. To extend what a mode *can do*, the backend chain is `PaymentModeResource` → `PaymentModeService` → `PaymentModeDAO` → `Bill.hbm.xml`, mirrored on the frontend by `types/index.ts` and the payment-mode form modal.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
